{"name":"Sonoran Desert","hex":"#cfb8a1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sonoran Desert","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A desert which covers large parts of the southwestern United States in Arizona and California, and of Northwestern Mexico."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sonoran_Desert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sonoran Desert","blocks":[{"text":"The Sonoran Desert is a hot desert and ecoregion in North America that covers parts of the northwestern Mexican states of Sonora, Baja California, and Baja California Sur, as well as part of the Southwestern United States. It has an area of 260,000 square kilometers (100,000 sq mi)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Saguaro_National_Park_-_Flickr_-_Joe_Parks.jpg/330px-Saguaro_National_Park_-_Flickr_-_Joe_Parks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonoran_Desert","wikidata":"Q189429"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert","wikidata":"Q8514"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Sonoradesert_1.JPG/500px-Sonoradesert_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Sonoradesert_1.JPG/1280px-Sonoradesert_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Sonoradesert_1.JPG/500px-Sonoradesert_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Sonoran Desert near Tucson, Arizona during winter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASonoradesert_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg/500px-Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg/1280px-Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg/500px-Prosopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Velvet mesquite (Prosopis velutina)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProsopis_velutina_Anza-Borrego.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Washingtonia_fi